---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import schema from '../data/schema/what-is-vvp.json';
---
<Layout
  title="What is Variable Video Production (VVP)? | Flipick"
  description="Variable Video Production (VVP) is a technique where one master video is rendered into thousands of unique, personalised versions — each with different names, offers, stores or languages — without re-recording."
  keywords="variable video production, VVP, what is VVP, personalized video at scale, AI video personalization, one master video many versions, VVP vs personalized video"
  ogType="article"
  page="what-is-vvp"
  schema={schema}
>
  <main>

  <!-- ================= HERO ================= -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="hero-grid rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">VVP Explained &middot; Flipick Knowledge Base</span>
        <h1 class="hero-h1-fluid">What is Variable Video <span class="serif-i">Production (VVP)?</span></h1>
        <div class="vvp-def-block">
          <p class="sub"><strong>Variable Video Production (VVP) is a technique where a single master video film is rendered into thousands of unique, personalised versions &mdash; each containing different data values such as a viewer&rsquo;s name, store address, renewal date, local offer, language or product &mdash; without re-recording or re-rendering the underlying footage.</strong> Each variant is delivered via a unique authenticated link, and viewing behaviour (completion, drop-off, CTA clicks) is tracked per recipient. VVP lets brands send one message at scale while making every viewer feel it was produced for them alone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/vvp-usa">See VVP in action</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" data-demo-link href="https://calendly.com/amol-chandsarkar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a demo</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= IN A SENTENCE ================= -->
  <section class="section-pad-band">
    <div class="lwrap">
      <div class="slim-band rv">
        <div class="slim-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">The 10-second version</span>
          <h2>One film. Thousands of recipients. Every version unique.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <div class="st"><b>1</b><span>master film, produced once at full AI render cost</span></div>
          <div class="st"><b>1,000s</b><span>of personalised variants, each at a fraction of the master&rsquo;s cost</span></div>
          <div class="st"><b>100%</b><span>viewing tracked — per recipient, not just in aggregate</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= HOW IT WORKS ================= -->
  <section id="how" class="ps-section-top section-white">
    <div class="lwrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">How It Works</span>
        <h2>Four steps from brief to <span class="serif-i text-brand">every inbox.</span></h2>
        <p>VVP separates the expensive, creative step (producing the master film) from the inexpensive, data-driven step (producing variants from it). The master is rendered once at full quality using Flipick&rsquo;s AI studio pipeline. Every variant is then generated by overlaying personalised data fields &mdash; names, prices, addresses, languages &mdash; on top of that fixed master, without touching the underlying footage. This keeps variant cost at roughly 1&ndash;5% of the master&rsquo;s cost, even at 10,000+ recipients.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ps-proc rv">
        <div class="ps-pc">
          <div class="ps-pc-n">01</div>
          <h3>Brief and screenplay</h3>
          <p>Define the campaign objective and the data fields each recipient will see. Flipick&rsquo;s AI converts the brief into a screenplay and storyboard for approval.</p>
          <div class="ps-pc-detail">Brief &rarr; screenplay &rarr; storyboard approval</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ps-pc">
          <div class="ps-pc-n">02</div>
          <h3>Render the master film</h3>
          <p>The approved storyboard becomes a studio-grade AI film &mdash; consistent characters, branded overlays, voiceover. This is the single paid AI render.</p>
          <div class="ps-pc-detail">Full AI render &middot; charged once</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ps-pc">
          <div class="ps-pc-n">03</div>
          <h3>Generate variants from data</h3>
          <p>Upload your data file (CSV or API feed). Each row becomes one variant: name, store, offer, language, price &mdash; composited on the master on Flipick&rsquo;s servers.</p>
          <div class="ps-pc-detail">No re-recording &middot; minutes per batch</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ps-pc">
          <div class="ps-pc-n">04</div>
          <h3>Distribute and track</h3>
          <p>Each recipient gets a unique authenticated link. Flipick tracks who watched, for how long, and whether they clicked the CTA &mdash; per viewer, not per campaign.</p>
          <div class="ps-pc-detail">Per-recipient tracking &middot; audit-ready</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ================= USE CASES ================= -->
  <section class="ps-section">
    <div class="lwrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">Where VVP Is Used</span>
        <h2>Industries that send the same message <span class="serif-i text-brand">to many people differently.</span></h2>
        <p>Any organisation that communicates a repeated message to a list of named recipients &mdash; where the message needs something specific to each person to land &mdash; is a natural fit for VVP.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid3 rv" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>Retail &amp; FMCG</h3>
          <p><strong>Use case: per-store promotional video.</strong> A retailer with 200 stores sends one festive offer video. Each store&rsquo;s variant shows that store&rsquo;s name, address, opening hours and local pricing &mdash; produced from a single master in minutes. No per-store agency brief needed.</p>
          <a href="/vvp-india" class="link-inherit">See VVP for Indian retail &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>Automotive Dealer Groups</h3>
          <p><strong>Use case: rooftop-level offer video.</strong> A dealer group runs a Labor Day promotion. Each rooftop gets its own video with its store name, address, offer details and contact number &mdash; generated from the group-level brief in an afternoon. No per-dealership production needed.</p>
          <a href="/dealership" class="link-inherit">See VVP for dealer groups &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>BFSI &amp; Insurance</h3>
          <p><strong>Use case: policy renewal and onboarding.</strong> An insurer sends 50,000 renewal reminders. Each video addresses the policyholder by name, shows their policy number, renewal date and specific plan details &mdash; authenticated so only that recipient can open it. Completion is tracked per policy.</p>
          <a href="/vvp-usa" class="link-inherit">See VVP live demo &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>Enterprise L&amp;D</h3>
          <p><strong>Use case: role-specific compliance training.</strong> An L&amp;D team sends the same compliance module to every employee &mdash; but each video addresses the learner by name and references their role, department and jurisdiction. Completion is tracked per learner, not per cohort.</p>
          <a href="/ai-video-ld" class="link-inherit">See AI Video for L&amp;D &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>Telecom &amp; Utilities</h3>
          <p><strong>Use case: plan upgrade and renewal.</strong> A telecom operator sends 100,000 personalised upgrade videos. Each shows the customer&rsquo;s current plan, the upgrade offer and the deadline &mdash; tailored by region, usage tier and language. Click-throughs are tracked per subscriber.</p>
          <a href="/vvp-usa" class="link-inherit">See VVP for communications &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>Marketing &amp; Performance</h3>
          <p><strong>Use case: account-based marketing (ABM).</strong> A B2B marketing team sends prospect-specific videos. Each video mentions the prospect&rsquo;s company name, industry pain point and a tailored offer &mdash; making cold outreach feel like a bespoke pitch. Reply rates typically outperform email-only sequences by 3&ndash;5&times;.</p>
          <a href="/ai-video-platform" class="link-inherit">See the AI Video Platform &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ================= VVP VS TRADITIONAL ================= -->
  <section class="ps-section">
    <div class="lwrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">VVP vs Traditional Video</span>
        <h2>Why not just produce a version for each <span class="serif-i text-brand">recipient?</span></h2>
        <p>The short answer: cost and speed. Traditional personalised video &mdash; where each variant is generated individually by an AI engine &mdash; works for small lists but becomes uneconomical at hundreds or thousands of recipients. VVP solves this with a fundamentally different architecture.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ps-ba-grid rv">
        <div class="ps-ba-card before">
          <div class="ps-ba-head">Traditional per-recipient AI video</div>
          <h3>Generate a new video for every person</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Each recipient gets a fresh AI generation</li>
            <li>Generation cost multiplies with list size</li>
            <li>Quality and character consistency vary between runs</li>
            <li>Render time scales linearly &mdash; 1,000 recipients = 1,000 renders</li>
            <li>No guaranteed brand consistency across variants</li>
            <li>Practical ceiling: tens or low hundreds of recipients</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ps-ba-card after">
          <div class="ps-ba-head">Flipick VVP</div>
          <h3>Render once, compose thousands of times</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>One studio-grade master film, rendered once</li>
            <li>Each variant composites data over the fixed master &mdash; no re-rendering</li>
            <li>Identical characters, lighting and brand consistency across all variants</li>
            <li>Variant generation time: minutes per batch regardless of list size</li>
            <li>Per-variant cost: roughly 1&ndash;5% of the master&rsquo;s cost</li>
            <li>Practical ceiling: unlimited. 1 or 1,000,000 recipients, same architecture</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ================= VVP VS GENERIC PERSONALISED VIDEO ================= -->
  <section class="ps-section section-white">
    <div class="lwrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">VVP vs Generic Personalised Video</span>
        <h2>Not all &ldquo;personalised video&rdquo; <span class="serif-i text-brand">is the same.</span></h2>
        <p>Several tools claim personalised video. VVP as Flipick implements it is a specific, production-grade technique &mdash; not a low-quality name-insertion feature bolted onto existing video tools.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid2 rv" style="margin-top:2rem">
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>Simple name-insertion tools</h3>
          <p>Overlay a first name on a generic template. No real production value. Every recipient sees the same footage with a text field swapped. Works for birthday cards; doesn&rsquo;t work for financial services, automotive or regulated-industry communications where the content itself must differ per recipient.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>Flipick VVP</h3>
          <p>Overlay any data &mdash; names, addresses, prices, dates, languages, product codes &mdash; on a studio-grade, brand-approved master film. Authenticated delivery (only the intended recipient opens the video). Per-recipient tracking of completion, drop-off and CTA. Built for regulated industries, enterprise L&amp;D and high-stakes customer communications.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>AI video re-generators (Synthesia, HeyGen per-variant)</h3>
          <p>Re-run the AI generation engine for each variant. Produces fresh video per recipient but at full AI render cost each time. Character consistency and brand fidelity degrade across runs. Economically viable for small lists (&lt;50), not for thousands of recipients.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>What makes Flipick VVP different</h3>
          <p>Flipick is the only platform that covers the full pipeline: <strong>Create</strong> (brief &rarr; screenplay &rarr; storyboard &rarr; master film), <strong>Distribute</strong> (VVP variant generation &rarr; authenticated delivery), and <strong>Prove</strong> (per-recipient authenticated tracking, completion, CTA analytics). No other tool does all three in one workflow.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider">

  <!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
  <section class="ps-section" id="faq">
    <div class="lwrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</span>
        <h2>What people ask about <span class="serif-i text-brand">VVP.</span></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="rv">
        <details class="dlr-fq">
          <summary>What is Variable Video Production (VVP)?</summary>
          <p>Variable Video Production (VVP) is a technique where a single master video is rendered into thousands of unique, personalised versions &mdash; each containing different data values such as a viewer&rsquo;s name, store address, renewal date, local offer, language or product &mdash; without re-recording or re-rendering the underlying footage. Flipick delivers each version via a unique authenticated link so only the intended recipient can open it, and viewing behaviour (completion, drop-off, CTA clicks) is tracked individually.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dlr-fq">
          <summary>How is VVP different from traditional personalised video?</summary>
          <p>Traditional personalised video tools render a separate AI-generated video for every recipient &mdash; which is slow and expensive at scale. Flipick&rsquo;s VVP renders one studio-grade master film once (at full AI render cost), then produces every variant by compositing data overlays and voice swaps on top of that master at a small fraction of the original cost. At 1,000 recipients, the per-video cost for a VVP variant is roughly 1&ndash;5% of the master&rsquo;s cost.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dlr-fq">
          <summary>What can be personalised in a VVP video?</summary>
          <p>Anything that can be expressed as a data field: the viewer&rsquo;s name, account number or policy ID; store name, address and phone number; current offer price or expiry date; vehicle make, model and colour; language of narration and on-screen text; and any brand overlay such as a logo, CTA button or legal disclaimer. Fields are defined in a data file (CSV or API feed) and each row becomes one variant.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dlr-fq">
          <summary>Which industries use Variable Video Production?</summary>
          <p>VVP is widely used in retail (per-store promotional videos), automotive (dealer co-op campaigns and rooftop-level offer videos), BFSI (policy renewal reminders, loan disbursement notifications and KYC onboarding), telecom (personalised plan upgrade or renewal videos), and enterprise L&amp;D (role-specific onboarding and compliance training delivered to each learner&rsquo;s inbox).</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dlr-fq">
          <summary>How long does it take to produce a VVP campaign?</summary>
          <p>The master film follows Flipick&rsquo;s standard AI video workflow: brief to approved screenplay and storyboard (same day), rendering the master film (hours). Variant generation for any number of recipients takes minutes per batch. A full VVP campaign &mdash; master plus 1,000 variants &mdash; typically goes from brief to distribution-ready in 5&ndash;7 business days.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dlr-fq">
          <summary>Can VVP videos be tracked?</summary>
          <p>Yes. Every VVP variant is delivered via a unique authenticated link tied to a named recipient. Flipick tracks who opened the video, how far they watched, whether they clicked the CTA, and from which device &mdash; per recipient, not just in aggregate. This audit-ready data is available for compliance-grade reporting in regulated industries.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="dlr-fq">
          <summary>Is VVP the same as &ldquo;virtual video production&rdquo;?</summary>
          <p>No. &ldquo;Virtual video production&rdquo; refers to using LED walls or CGI environments as physical production backdrops &mdash; a filmmaking technique. Variable Video Production (VVP) is a post-production and distribution technology: it takes a finished master film and produces thousands of data-driven personalised variants from it. The two terms describe different things in different industries.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= INTERNAL LINKS ================= -->
  <section class="ps-section-top">
    <div class="lwrap">
      <div class="sec-head rv">
        <span class="eyebrow">Explore VVP on Flipick</span>
        <h2>See it live, or learn more about <span class="serif-i text-brand">how we build it.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid3 rv" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>VVP Live Demo (US)</h3>
          <p>Try the live API-driven VVP demo: enter a store address and phone number and watch a personalised retail video render in under 60 seconds.</p>
          <a href="/vvp-usa" class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-top:1rem;display:inline-block">Try the demo &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>VVP for India</h3>
          <p>How VVP is used in India: festive retail campaigns, regional languages, and per-store variants for brands with large distributor or dealer networks.</p>
          <a href="/vvp-india" class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-top:1rem;display:inline-block">See VVP India &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="fcard">
          <h3>AI Video Platform</h3>
          <p>VVP is one capability inside Flipick&rsquo;s full AI video platform &mdash; from brief to authenticated proof of viewing, all in one workflow.</p>
          <a href="/ai-video-platform" class="btn btn-ghost" style="margin-top:1rem;display:inline-block">See the platform &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= CLOSING CTA ================= -->
  <section class="closing" aria-label="Call to action">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Ready to see VVP with <span class="serif-i">your own brief?</span></h2>
      <p>In 15 minutes we&rsquo;ll show you how one of your campaigns would scale to every recipient, size and language &mdash; and what it would cost.</p>
      <div class="ctas-center">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" data-demo-link href="https://calendly.com/amol-chandsarkar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a demo</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  </main>

  <script is:inline slot="scripts">
    (function() {
      var els = document.querySelectorAll('.rv');
      if (!els.length) return;
      var io = new IntersectionObserver(function(entries) {
        entries.forEach(function(e) { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); } });
      }, { threshold: 0.1 });
      els.forEach(function(el) { io.observe(el); });
      setTimeout(function() { els.forEach(function(el) { el.classList.add('in'); }); }, 3000);
    })();
  </script>
</Layout>
